  "definition": "A neurofibroma is a benign, moderately firm, encapsulated tumor made up of overgrowth of Schwann cells and fibroblasts that includes parts of nerve fibers. It usually develops along peripheral or cranial nerves and is a central feature of neurofibromatosis type 1.",
